\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.8}{\ignorespaces Top panel: the set of modes that could be present at the SRM is shown by the black-purple-orange-white curve, as described in chapter \ref  {chapter:simulation_finesse}. The purple region shows which modes can reach 98\% mode matching by using the the AWC in HAM6. The orange cross indicates the mode that corresponds to the SRC having a single pass Gouy phase of 21.3\si {\degree }. The contours indicate the mode matching between the arm mode and the OMC mode.  Bottom panel: this shows the same modes as the top panel, except they have been transformed to the plane of the OMC waist. The target region is highlighted with a hatched area.\relax }}{40}{figure.caption.52}}
\newlabel{fig:bhdforligochapterlayout5fmodessrmomcmodematchingsuccess}{{2.8}{40}{Top panel: the set of modes that could be present at the SRM is shown by the black-purple-orange-white curve, as described in chapter \ref {chapter:simulation_finesse}. The purple region shows which modes can reach 98\% mode matching by using the the AWC in HAM6. The orange cross indicates the mode that corresponds to the SRC having a single pass Gouy phase of 21.3\si {\degree }. The contours indicate the mode matching between the arm mode and the OMC mode.\\ Bottom panel: this shows the same modes as the top panel, except they have been transformed to the plane of the OMC waist. The target region is highlighted with a hatched area.\relax }{figure.caption.52}{}}
